  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Definitive Healthcare’s core subscription revenue continues to contract, and a shrinking deferred revenue balance points to persisting demand softness in its primary offering. The professional services line is a bright spot, growing briskly as clients seek project-based work, but this mix shift toward lower-recurring revenue may dampen visibility. Despite these headwinds, the company exceeded market expectations for the quarter, suggesting the underlying end-market need for healthcare commercial intelligence remains, even if purchasing patterns have turned cautious.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership is countering top-line pressure with rigorous cost discipline, delivering margin expansion and strong free cash flow conversion. They consistently provided achievable guidance, hit the upper end of revenue ranges, and beat earnings consensus, reinforcing operational credibility. The emphasis on profitability and cash generation, together with a steady outlook for the next quarter and full year, signals a pragmatic playbook focused on sustaining financial health while the subscription base stabilizes.",
